### 13. Notion MCP

{% logo src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/devanshug2307/agentskills-blog-content/main/images/best-mcp-servers-for-developers-2026/logos/notion-mcp.png" name="Notion MCP" size=40 /%}


**What it is:** Notion's hosted MCP server at `https://mcp.notion.com/mcp`. Notion's developer docs say it lets an assistant search your workspace, create and edit pages and manage databases. Notion documents manual setup for Codex, Claude Code, Cursor, Hermes, VS Code and others, and says it will retire the legacy SSE endpoint, with a migration guide.

**Who it is for:** developers whose specs, runbooks and meeting notes live in Notion.

**Key features:** semantic workspace search, Markdown-native page reading and editing, and OAuth that respects each user's existing permissions, according to the notice in Notion's own local-server repo (vendor claim).

**Pros:**

- OAuth with no tokens to paste or pages to share by hand.
- Less token spend than the old local server, per Notion's comparison table (vendor-reported).
- Notion documents admin controls for MCP clients, including an enterprise-managed authorization page.

**Cons:**

- We did not verify rate limits or which roles can connect, so check Notion's help center before rolling it out to a team.
- Your agent gets what your Notion account can see, so a broad account means broad reach.
- The old self-hosted `makenotion/notion-mcp-server` repo (4,729 stars, MIT) says it is "no longer actively maintained or supported" and may be sunset. Do not start new work on it.

**Benefits for you:** the agent reads the spec before it writes the code.

**Pricing (as of November 27, 2026):** Free $0, Plus $10 per seat per month, Business $20 per seat per month. The MCP server has no separate fee listed.

**Standout use case:** turn a PRD page into an implementation plan and tracked tasks.

**Skip it if:** your docs live elsewhere, or you wanted the old local server.

**Setup:**

```bash
