## Best for X: decision table

| If you need | Pick | Why |
| --- | --- | --- |
| One server to start with | GitHub MCP | Covers issues, PRs and CI; read-only mode available |
| Fewer outdated API calls | Context7 | Two lookup tools, free tier |
| The agent to test its own UI | Playwright MCP | Cross-browser, no vision model |
| Console, network and traces | Chrome DevTools MCP | Real Chrome, performance insights |
| Start debugging from a stack trace | Sentry MCP | Project scoping, OAuth |
| Schema and migrations on Supabase | Supabase MCP | Migrations, logs, advisors, read-only option |
| Query tuning on any Postgres | Postgres MCP | Restricted mode, index tuning |
| Infra on Cloudflare | Cloudflare MCP | Whole API behind two tools |
| Deployments on Vercel | Vercel MCP | Logs and deployments from the session |
| Tickets next to the code | Linear MCP | Read-only endpoint and team scoping |
| Payments work with guardrails | Stripe MCP | Sandbox and live permissions set separately |
| Design to code | Figma Dev Mode MCP | Variables and components as input |
| Specs and runbooks | Notion MCP | OAuth with existing permissions |
| Governed local servers | Docker MCP Toolkit | Signed images, CPU and memory limits |
| Terminal and files in a chat client | Desktop Commander | Process control and filesystem tools |

## Common mistakes

1. **Installing all 15.** Every connected server adds tool definitions to the context of every request. The Playwright README itself warns that its schemas and snapshots are heavy. Start with the two or three that match your stack.
2. **Leaving write access on while you explore.** GitHub, Linear and Supabase each have a documented read-only path. Use it until the agent has earned more.
3. **Giving an agent a live-mode Stripe or production database connection.** Use a Stripe sandbox, and a development Supabase project or Postgres MCP restricted mode.
4. **Trusting the text the agent reads.** Issues, PR comments, Sentry events and Notion pages are untrusted input. They can carry instructions aimed at your agent. Keep approvals on for write tools.
5. **Installing the archived Postgres reference server.** Its repo is archived and its npm package is deprecated. Use Postgres MCP Pro or your vendor's server.
6. **Starting new work on Notion's old local server.** Notion says it is no longer actively maintained.
7. **Ignoring rate limits.** Figma's Starter plan allows 20 tool calls a month; Context7's free plan blocks after 1,000 calls a month.
8. **Forgetting the Stripe key deadline.** From January 11, 2027, full-access secret keys and non-agent restricted keys stop working with Stripe MCP.

## Setup checklist

1. List the three jobs your agent does most (for example: read tickets, test the UI, check production errors).
2. Pick one server per job from the decision table.
3. Prefer a hosted OAuth server where one exists, and a local server only when you need local data.
4. Turn on read-only or restricted mode first, and scope to one project, team or repository.
5. Use a sandbox account for payments and a development project for databases.
6. Keep your client's approval prompts on for any tool that writes or spends.
7. Check your client's own MCP docs for the config file format; Codex uses TOML, others use JSON.
8. Review the connected tool list after setup and remove tools you will not use.
9. Check each vendor's changelog every few weeks: several of these servers shipped releases within days of this post.

## How we evaluated

**What we did.** On November 27, 2026 we read each vendor's own documentation and pricing page, pulled stars, licenses, release tags and last-push dates from the GitHub API, read the READMEs for Playwright MCP, Chrome DevTools MCP, GitHub MCP, Context7, Postgres MCP and Desktop Commander, and checked the status of the archived reference servers with the GitHub API and `npm view`. We confirmed that every internal and AgentPedia link returns HTTP 200, that the YouTube ids resolve through oEmbed, and that the X post ids resolve through the syndication endpoint with the expected author.

**What we did not do.** We did not install or run any of these servers for this post, so we make no claim about speed, accuracy or token use beyond what the vendors state, and those vendor numbers are labeled as such. We did not test any client and server pairing in the works-with matrix. We did not benchmark servers against each other, and we are not aware of a neutral benchmark that covers these 15.

**Ranking.** The order is our judgment of how broadly each server helps a working developer, with GitHub, docs lookup and browser verification first because they apply to almost every project. Servers tied to one vendor (Sentry, Supabase, Cloudflare, Vercel, Linear, Stripe, Figma, Notion) rank by how many developers use that vendor and by how well the vendor documents controls. We have no affiliate relationship with any vendor listed.

**Known gaps.** The full list of tools for several servers was not read end to end, and a few prices depend on a billing toggle on the vendor's page (see the notes under each pricing line). Check the vendor's page before you buy.

## FAQ

### What are the best MCP servers for developers in 2026?

For most developers, start with GitHub MCP for source control, Context7 for current docs, and Playwright MCP or Chrome DevTools MCP for browser verification. Add vendor servers (Sentry, Supabase, Vercel, Cloudflare, Linear, Stripe, Figma, Notion) only for services you already use.

### What are the best MCP servers for Claude Code?

Everything in this list is documented for Claude Code except where the works-with matrix says "Standard transport" (Postgres MCP's README names Cursor only). Claude Code supports local stdio, remote HTTP and SSE servers. For a Claude Code-specific ranking see [AgentPedia's list](https://agentpedia.codes/blog/best-mcp-servers-claude-code).

### Are MCP servers free?

Many are. Playwright MCP, Chrome DevTools MCP, Postgres MCP and Desktop Commander are free and open source. GitHub MCP, Supabase MCP, Vercel MCP and Linear MCP show no separate server fee, but they connect to services that have paid plans. Context7 has a free plan limited to 1,000 calls a month. Figma's free tier is 20 calls a month.

### What is the difference between a remote and a local MCP server?

A remote server is hosted by the vendor and you connect with a URL, usually through OAuth. A local server is a process your client starts on your machine, through `npx` or Docker. Remote is easier and stays current; local keeps traffic on your machine and puts update and credential handling on you.

### Is the Postgres MCP server archived?

The original Postgres reference server is. It now lives in `modelcontextprotocol/servers-archived`, GitHub marks that repo archived (last push May 28, 2025), and the npm package carries a deprecation message that says it is archived and unmaintained with no security guarantees. This post uses Crystal DBA's Postgres MCP Pro, which was pushed on November 26, 2026.

### Which MCP server is safest to start with?

Context7 (two lookup tools) and GitHub MCP in read-only mode are the lowest-risk starting points in this list. Anything that writes, spends or runs commands (Desktop Commander, Stripe MCP, Supabase MCP, Cloudflare MCP) needs scoping and approvals.

### Do MCP servers work with Codex, Cursor and Gemini CLI, not just Claude Code?

Yes. The protocol is client-agnostic, and each of the six clients in our matrix documents local and remote server support. Vendor docs name Claude Code and Cursor most often, then Codex; Gemini CLI, OpenCode and Hermes appear less often, so check the works-with matrix above and the vendor's page.

### How many MCP servers should I connect at once?

As few as cover your daily jobs. Each server adds tool definitions to every request, and Playwright's own README says CLI plus skills can be more token-efficient than its MCP server. Hermes and other clients can filter a server's tools to only the ones you need.

### Is Playwright MCP or Chrome DevTools MCP better?

Playwright MCP is better for cross-browser flows, Chrome DevTools MCP for performance traces and network inspection in Chrome. Many teams use both. See the head-to-head above.

### What changed in Stripe MCP recently?

Stripe labels it a public preview. OAuth sessions expire after 14 days. From January 11, 2027, Stripe says MCP will no longer accept full-access secret keys or non-agent restricted API keys, so migrate to an agent API key or OAuth.

### Does Notion still have a local MCP server?

The `makenotion/notion-mcp-server` repo still exists (MIT, 4,729 stars, last pushed October 29, 2026), but its README says it is no longer actively maintained or supported and may be sunset, and points users to Notion's hosted remote MCP server.

### Are MCP servers safe to use with production data?

Not by default. Vendors warn about this themselves: Supabase's docs open with a security warning, Vercel notes the agent gets the same access as your user, and Desktop Commander's README says its guardrails are not a sandbox. Use read-only modes, development projects and sandboxes, and keep approval prompts on.

### Where can I find skills that pair with these servers?

See the catalog block above, with 15 entries linked to agentskills.codes, and our posts on [Claude Code skills](https://agentskills.codes/blog/best-claude-code-skills-for-developers-2026) and [Codex skills](https://agentskills.codes/blog/best-codex-skills-2026).

